1
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:07,800
P'Dan.

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,400
Hm.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,900
Thanks.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,380
For helping me see the project through.

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,180
Actually...

6
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,680
I'm pretty good at what I do.

7
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,040
So I figured...

8
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,480
I'd share some of that talent with everyone else.

9
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:25,160
Yes, Mr. Talented.

10
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,240
And the way you're looking at me...

11
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:32,080
Is there something you wanna tell me?

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,620
Well...

13
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:40,940
A startup reached out to me.

14
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:42,880
They offered me a job.

15
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:45,720
The benefits are pretty good.

16
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:46,740
And the pay's not bad either.

17
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,360
Oh, nice!

18
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,340
Congrats, P'Dan.

19
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:58,280
It's just... really far away, Pond.

20
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,000
Why?

21
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:05,480
What do you think...

22
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:08,420
you'll do after you graduate?

23
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,040
Me? After I graduate?

24
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,160
I guess I'll get a job.

25
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,140
I wanna save up a lot of money.

26
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:17,480
And maybe move down south.

27
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,480
I'd like to work in fisheries.

28
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,600
I'm sick of the mountains. I wanna live by the sea for a change.

29
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,320
What if...

30
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:29,520
I had to take a job somewhere far away from you, Pond?

31
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,160
How would you feel about that?

32
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:34,900
What am I supposed to say?

33
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:37,140
It's your future, Dan.

34
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,820
What about us?

35
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,420
Us?

36
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:45,860
I mean...

37
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,280
Our future.

38
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,080
I haven't really thought that far ahead about us, Dan.

39
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,320
I just wanna graduate...

40
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,800
and get a job.

41
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:59,800
I wanna chase my own dreams.

42
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:04,060
I don't wanna live up north anymore.

43
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,820
I wanna...

44
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,440
live by the sea and work in fisheries.

45
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:11,180
Cruise along the beach in a sports car... that kinda thing.

46
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,780
Honestly? I love that.

47
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,400
Oh...

48
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,960
I've got plans with my friends today.

49
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:22,180
So I'm gonna head out, P'Dan.

50
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,180
There's a party. A party!

51
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,300
See you around, bro.

52
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:26,420
Thanks.

53
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,140
Dan.

54
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:19,840
Good Lord.

55
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,260
You work this hard...

56
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:26,280
Are you saving up to put a ring on Baby's finger or something?

57
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,260
What, boss?

58
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:30,620
I told you this morning, I'm not focusing on that stuff.

59
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:33,580
Jeez, you're way too serious.

60
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:37,420
Ease up a little. Work, work, work... sometimes you gotta...

61
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:44,240
make room for love. That's what gives life a little flavor.

62
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,520
But if we're talking about...

63
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,500
the flavor of my love life, it'd probably be bitter.

64
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:50,680
See?

65
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:55,060
A few heartbreaks and you're just gonna bury yourself in work?

66
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:57,840
Auntie Som-O's got a point.

67
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,280
Dan's been heartbroken for a whole year.

68
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,940
You should try opening your heart to someone else.

69
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,800
You're taking her side too?

70
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,920
Oh, come on.

71
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,780
At our age...

72
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:09,340
sitting around doing nothing but work

73
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:13,520
is just wasting your time and energy.

74
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,340
Go work that charm of yours once in a while.

75
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:19,080
It's not like I wanna work all the time. I just have deadlines.

76
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,940
Yeah, yeah, I get the deadlines.

77
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,780
But where...

78
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,060
is your boss?

79
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:27,360
Our boss hasn't gone anywhere.

80
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,380
Best has a new intern today.

81
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,480
So he's off taking care of him.

82
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,900
How do you know everything?

83
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,180
Well, I...

84
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,860
I mean...

85
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,960
I don't know.

86
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,820
That's suspicious.

87
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,280
Everyone.

88
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,400
Perfect timing. We're all here.

89
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,040
I'd like to introduce our new intern.

90
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,360
He'll be joining our department.

91
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,760
Since we're all here, I'll introduce him now.

92
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:01,180
This is Auntie Som-O, head of PM.

93
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:03,860
Hi, guys!

94
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,480
And this is Tontae.

95
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:06,780
And this...

96
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,400
is Dan.

97
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,960
And this is Pond.

98
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,020
Hi.

99
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:13,040
I'm Pond.

100
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,600
I'm the new intern.

101
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,680
Nice to meet you all. Please take care of me.

102
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,720
What the...!?

103
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:23,140
Oh!

104
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:24,340
You two know each other?

105
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:27,020
Well then, Dan, I'll leave Pond in your care.

106
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:28,760
But I...

107
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,280
Perfect.

108
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,020
I'd love to intern with Dan.

109
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:54,320
Whoa, Dan.

110
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,720
I know you missed me.

111
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:59,020
But you don't have to get all shy about it.

112
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,840
Or maybe...

113
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:05,180
you're just happy to see me?

114
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,960
How the hell did you get here?

115
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,300
Did you follow me?

116
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,700
Me?

117
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,540
Why would I follow you?

118
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,020
Then why are you here?

119
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,620
If you're not gonna tell me...

120
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:23,980
I'm supposed to be the one explaining?

121
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,080
Fine. I'll tell you.

122
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,160
My professor told me to find an internship.

123
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,300
So I came here.

124
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,040
But there are tons of other places.

125
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:36,600
Why can't I intern here?

126
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,500
So you want everyone to know...

127
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,880
that you and I used to...

128
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,000
Don't worry. I won't tell anyone.

129
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:48,220
That you...

130
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,640
used to like me that much.

131
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:55,240
You little...

132
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,940
Man, this office is way up there.

133
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,540
Come on. Think of it as morning exercise.

134
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:46,300
Morning, boys!

135
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:49,900
Here to brighten up your morning!

136
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:58,620
What are you looking at?

137
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,500
Nothing.

138
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,120
Something feels weird.

139
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,500
Like I can smell something... funky.

140
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:12,760
Everyone.

141
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,380
I'm gonna take the work we put together

142
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:17,060
and show it to Mr. Ton first.

143
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,500
I'll help you, bro.

144
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,420
No need. It's only a few plans.

145
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,200
It's fine. I'll carry them.

146
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,320
You already finished your work?

147
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,140
Yeah, I just finished.

148
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,560
Sorry, boss.

149
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,220
Sorry, bro.

150
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:40,260
Come on. I'll carry them.

151
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,440
Does he really have to be this obvious?

152
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,520
When the hell did he finish all that?

153
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,940
I got here before him.

154
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,860
And I still haven't finished mine.

155
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,820
Guess I'm the last one here.

156
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,040
So... what should I do first?

157
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,420
As my mentor...

158
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:09,180
you're supposed to teach me.

159
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:10,460
Uh...

160
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,160
Are you gonna teach me or not?

161
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,820
Nope.

162
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,740
Yes, Mom.

163
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:32,020
Oh, that? I've already talked to them.

164
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,360
Yeah.

165
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:35,780
Mom...

166
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,760
Why did Benz go on vacation without taking Tin-Tin?

167
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,740
If I'm supposed to babysit Tin-Tin...

168
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,180
I'm not doing it, Mom.

169
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,900
And if you wanna come stay at the condo with Tin-Tin...

170
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:45,860
then just come.

171
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:47,440
I'll find somewhere else to stay.

172
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,220
Okay.

173
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,120
Sorry, Best.

174
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:56,900
Um...

175
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,620
I couldn't help overhearing...

176
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:01,440
you're having trouble finding a place to stay, right?

177
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:03,980
A little.

178
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:05,040
Well...

179
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,900
My mom and my niece are moving into my condo.

180
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,940
And I'm not exactly a kid person.

181
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:12,100
So I'll have to find somewhere else to stay.

182
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,280
I was wondering if Dan might have a spare room.

183
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,460
How about this?

184
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:18,200
I've got a spare room.

185
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,480
It's the room...

186
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,600
I used when I was in college.

187
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,880
But I don't live there anymore.

188
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,000
You could stay with...

189
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,700
I mean...

190
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,360
you could stay at my condo.

191
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,700
Are you sure, Tontae?

192
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,020
Of course.

193
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:34,160
If you're okay with it.

194
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,760
Uh...

195
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,400
Sure.

196
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,840
I'd really appreciate it.

197
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,120
My pleasure.

198
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:42,300
If Tontae's okay with it, I'm okay with it.

199
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,500
Then...

200
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:47,440
Whenever you're ready to move your stuff in, just let me know.

201
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,440
Uh...

202
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,800
How about tonight?

203
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,080
Tonight?

204
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:54,760
Sure.

205
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,300
Uh...

206
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,780
Sorry, are you heading upstairs?

207
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:01,700
Oh, right. I forgot.

208
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,260
Where are you going? / I'm heading upstairs too.

209
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:06,980
Go ahead.

210
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,980
Tonight, then.

211
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:12,800
Okay.

212
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:26,620
Dan.

213
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,500
I need your help with something.

214
00:12:28,940 --> 00:12:30,000
What's up?

215
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,780
Well...

216
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:34,460
Best's mom is moving into his condo, so now he doesn't have anywhere to stay.

217
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,920
I want Best to...

218
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,420
stay at my condo.

219
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:38,700
That's great.

220
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,360
If I live with Best...

221
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,500
we can split the rent.

222
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,200
And you'd have to pay me less, too.

223
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:47,500
I'm letting Best stay for free.

224
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,060
And...

225
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,680
he'll have the whole place to himself.

226
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:53,360
So...

227
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:55,940
You're really choosing him over me?

228
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,780
It's not like that.

229
00:12:57,780 --> 00:13:00,260
You know I've been trying to get with Best for a whole year.

230
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:03,860
And this is my one chance to get closer to him.

231
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,020
You said you'd help me, too.

232
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:07,840
But does it really have to go this far?

233
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:09,120
Or do I need to do even more?

234
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,560
Should I rent a whole house next?

235
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,200
Okay, okay. Enough.

236
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,140
Then where am I supposed to live?

237
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:18,100
Come live with me.

238
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,740
I seriously don't get Dan.

239
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:32,960
He's gone around the whole office asking everyone

240
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,740
if they have a spare room, but he never even asked me.

241
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,680
Don't take it personally, bro.

242
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:40,180
I think Dan...

243
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:41,900
probably just feels bad imposing on you.

244
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:44,400
Besides, Dan told me once...

245
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,860
that if he stayed around you all the time...

246
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,020
it'd feel like he was at work all the time.

247
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:51,100
Work? I'm just his boss.

248
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,980
I've been close with Daeng since high school.

249
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,860
Sure, we didn't go to the same university, but still.

250
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:58,160
Why would he feel awkward with me now?

251
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,680
I don't get it.

252
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,560
No one's free.

253
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,800
Nobody has a spare room.

254
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,880
Every room's taken.

255
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,760
Wow.

256
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,540
You've asked everyone in the whole office...

257
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,580
but never thought to ask this friend?

258
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,180
I could rent his room.

259
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:18,680
Then I'd have the place to myself.

260
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,320
I mean...

261
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,720
The place I'm staying now is pretty far.

262
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,580
It probably wouldn't be convenient for Dan.

263
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:29,720
Right, boss?

264
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:31,680
Yeah.

265
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:33,660
Far.

266
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,480
Not convenient.

267
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:37,040
Fine.

268
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:37,580
Yeah.

269
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,940
And the place that kid offered...

270
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,560
you turned that down too.

271
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,280
No.

272
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,860
I'm definitely not staying...

273
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,260
with that kid.

274
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:48,820
Wow, someone's playing hard to get.

275
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:50,820
He is pretty tiny and cute, though.

276
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,680
Did he tell you something?

277
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:55,500
No.

278
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:56,760
Um, I was just gonna say...

279
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:58,240
Pond's place has a spare room, bro.

280
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,660
And it's close to the office.

281
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:02,300
You'd save on commuting, too.

282
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:05,720
Still not taking it.

283
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:08,000
Then I'll stay at a hotel.

284
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,080
A hotel? Seriously?

285
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,540
With what money?

286
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:14,160
Daeng just spent a fortune getting that room renovated.

287
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,160
Ugh...

288
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,240
Easy, bro.

289
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,620
Breathe in.

290
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,120
And out.

291
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,860
Easy, bro.

292
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:31,800
Don't lose your temper. And don't get worked up, okay?

293
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,740
Don't worry about him.

294
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,020
Worry about yourself.

295
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:41,720
Come on. Let's go upstairs and get back to work.

296
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,280
Come on.

297
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:51,920
I still don't understand my friend.

298
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:54,420
Come on, boss. Take it easy.

299
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:02,960
That's all I can do for you.

300
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,060
Wow. You really kicked me to the curb.

301
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:08,620
I just wanted to take responsibility.

302
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:11,240
Your idea of taking responsibility is sending Best to the condo...

303
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,640
and making me live here?

304
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,880
Pond told me...

305
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,620
back when we were in college...

306
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:19,320
that you two used to sleep together, didn't you?

307
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,580
He told you that?

308
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,340
Or did I get it wrong?

309
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:29,880
I'm back.

310
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,240
The room's all ready.

311
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,560
Perfect, Pond.

312
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,280
I'm counting on you to look after Dan.

313
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:37,840
Bro.

314
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,020
I'm gonna go check on Best first.

315
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,920
Okay, bro.

316
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:41,880
See you.

317
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,740
Tontae...

318
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,800
The room's ready, Dan.

319
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,240
Where do you wanna stay?

320
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,060
You can pick.

321
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:54,880
Uh...

322
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:56,420
Actually...

323
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:58,640
Um...

324
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,260
I...

325
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,520
I just need a little corner of your room.

326
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,860
Just a little corner?

327
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:10,720
How about taking a little piece of my heart too?

328
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,480
Or maybe...

329
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:19,660
you want all of my heart?
